// src/Optimize/ReadersLogin2id.php, row 23
"There was a change in Reader management functionality in AA v2.8.1, so readers are not internally identified by their login, but by reader ID (item ID of reader in Reader slice). This is much more powerful - you can create relations just as in normal slice. It works well without any change. The only problem is, if you set any slice to be editable by users from Reader slice. In that case the fields edited_by........ and posted_by........ are filled by reader's login instead of reader id. You can fix it by \"Repair\"." => "AA v2.8.1\xA4\xC7\xC6\xC9\xBC\xD4\xB4\xC9\xCD\xFD\xB5\xA1\xC7\xBD\xA4\xCB\xCA\xD1\xB9\xB9\xA4\xAC\xA4\xA2\xA4\xEA\xA1\xA2\xC6\xC9\xBC\xD4\xA4\xCF\xC6\xE2\xC9\xF4\xC5\xAA\xA4\xCB\xA5\xED\xA5\xB0\xA5\xA4\xA5\xF3\xA4\xC7\xA4\xCF\xA4\xCA\xA4\xAF\xC6\xC9\xBC\xD4ID\xA1\xCA\xC6\xC9\xBC\xD4\xA5\xB9\xA5\xE9\xA5\xA4\xA5\xB9\xC6\xE2\xA4\xCE\xC6\xC9\xBC\xD4\xA4\xCE\xB9\xE0\xCC\xDCID\xA1\xCB\xA4\xC7\xBC\xB1\xCA\xCC\xA4\xB5\xA4\xEC\xA4\xEB\xA4\xE8\xA4\xA6\xA4\xCB\xA4\xCA\xA4\xEA\xA4\xDE\xA4\xB7\xA4\xBF\xA1\xA3\xA4\xB3\xA4\xEC\xA4\xCF\xA4\xCF\xA4\xEB\xA4\xAB\xA4\xCB\xB6\xAF\xCE\xCF\xA4\xC7\xA1\xA2\xC4\xCC\xBE\xEF\xA4\xCE\xA5\xB9\xA5\xE9\xA5\xA4\xA5\xB9\xA4\xC8\xC6\xB1\xCD\xCD\xA4\xCB\xB4\xD8\xB7\xB8\xA4\xF2\xBA\xEE\xC0\xAE\xA4\xC7\xA4\xAD\xA4\xDE\xA4\xB9\xA1\xA3\xCA\xD1\xB9\xB9\xA4\xCA\xA4\xB7\xA4\xC7\xCC\xE4\xC2\xEA\xA4\xCA\xA4\xAF\xC6\xB0\xBA\xEE\xA4\xB7\xA4\xDE\xA4\xB9\xA1\xA3\xCD\xA3\xB0\xEC\xA4\xCE\xCC\xE4\xC2\xEA\xA4\xCF\xA1\xA2\xC6\xC9\xBC\xD4\xA5\xB9\xA5\xE9\xA5\xA4\xA5\xB9\xA4\xCE\xCD\xF8\xCD\xD1\xBC\xD4\xA4\xAC\xCA\xD4\xBD\xB8\xA4\xC7\xA4\xAD\xA4\xEB\xA4\xE8\xA4\xA6\xA4\xCB\xA5\xB9\xA5\xE9\xA5\xA4\xA5\xB9\xA4\xF2\xC0\xDF\xC4\xEA\xA4\xB7\xA4\xC6\xA4\xA4\xA4\xEB\xBE\xEC\xB9\xE7\xA4\xC7\xA4\xB9\xA1\xA3\xA4\xBD\xA4\xCE\xBE\xEC\xB9\xE7\xA1\xA2edited_by........ \xA4\xC8 posted_by........ \xA4\xCE\xA5\xD5\xA5\xA3\xA1\xBC\xA5\xEB\xA5\xC9\xA4\xCB\xC6\xC9\xBC\xD4ID\xA4\xC7\xA4\xCF\xA4\xCA\xA4\xAF\xC6\xC9\xBC\xD4\xA4\xCE\xA5\xED\xA5\xB0\xA5\xA4\xA5\xF3\xA4\xAC\xC6